{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle (","type":"text"},{"code":"Bundle.module","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"your own","type":"text"}]},{"text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and add a ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"json","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overriding text per-app","anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, bypassing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSLocalizedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever) instead of the default:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builder closures (see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController"},{"text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself."}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"code":"Empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","role":"collection","title":"ScreenStates","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessi